<p>4. An intermediate used in the synthesis of perfumes is valeric acid, also called pentanoic acid. The \(pK_a\) of pentanoic acid is 4.84 at 25&deg;C.</p>

<ol start="1" style="list-style-type: lower-alpha;">
    <li>What is the \(pH\) of a 0.259 M solution of pentanoic acid?</li>
    <li>Sodium pentanoate is added to make a buffered solution. What is the pH of the solution if it is 0.210 M in sodium pentanoate?</li>
    <li>What is the final \(pH\) if 8.00 mL of 0.100 M HCl are added to 75.0 mL of the buffered solution?</li>
    <li>What is the final \(pH\) if 8.00 mL of 0.100 M NaOH are added to 75.0 mL of the buffered solution?</li>
</ol>

